In trying to really get a handle on the various places of different gismu,
I'm wondering what logic, if any, is present in the ordering of the places?
 I don't mean this to imply that the ordering isn't logical, I'm just
wondering if there are patterns I haven't noticed yet that might be helpful.
 E.g.:

For movement gismu, is origin always before destination?
For container gismu, is the thing contained always before the material of
the container?
Etc.

Are there patterns like this in the gismu structures that might help in
learning and memorizing?

Thanks,

Chris

